## Introduction

### What is JIRA?
- **JIRA** (originally "Java Issue Tracking Request Assessment") is a powerful issue and project tracking tool
- Developed by Atlassian, widely used by software development teams
- Supports tracking bugs, feature requests, tasks, and any other work items
- Available as Cloud, Server (deprecated), and Data Center versions

### Key Benefits
- **Centralized Issue Tracking**: All project issues in one place
- **Workflow Management**: Custom workflows for different issue types
- **Team Collaboration**: Comments, attachments, and notifications
- **Reporting and Analytics**: Track progress and metrics
- **Agile Support**: Native Scrum and Kanban board support
- **Integration**: Connect with Git, CI/CD, communication tools

### JIRA Editions
| Edition | Deployment | Best For |
|---------|-----------|----------|
| Cloud | SaaS | Small to medium teams, managed by Atlassian |
| Server | On-premise (Deprecated) | Legacy deployments |
| Data Center | On-premise | Large enterprises, high availability |

