## Best Practices

### Issue Management Best Practices

#### 1. Writing Clear Summaries
```
✅ "Login endpoint returns 500 error for duplicate emails"
❌ "Bug in login"

✅ "Add dark mode toggle to user settings"
❌ "UI improvement"

✅ "Database query timeout on reports page for datasets > 10k rows"
❌ "Performance issue"
```

#### 2. Detailed Descriptions
Include:
- Context and background
- Steps to reproduce (for bugs)
- Expected vs actual behavior
- Screenshots or logs
- Environment details

#### 3. Proper Prioritization
- Blocker: System down, no workaround
- High: Significant impact, affects multiple users
- Medium: Standard functionality
- Low: Nice to have, cosmetic

#### 4. Meaningful Labels
```
Use for cross-cutting concerns:
- #security
- #performance
- #accessibility
- #documentation
- #technical-debt
- #refactor
```

#### 5. Component Assignment
Organize by architecture:
- Frontend
- Backend
- API
- Database
- DevOps
- Documentation

### Sprint Planning Best Practices

#### 1. Capacity Planning
```
Team capacity = Number of developers × Hours available
Considering:
- Meetings (standups, planning, reviews)
- Support work
- Unexpected interruptions
Typically: 70-80% of theoretical capacity
```

#### 2. Story Sizing
- Don't make stories too large (max 13 points)
- Don't estimate too low (min 2 points)
- Leave time for testing and code review

#### 3. Sprint Commitment
- Commit only to definable work
- Leave 10-20% buffer for emergencies
- Don't overcommit based on optimism

#### 4. Definition of Done
```
Before marking issue as Done:
☐ Code written
☐ Code reviewed and approved
☐ Unit tests written (>80% coverage)
☐ Integration tests passed
☐ QA tested and approved
☐ Documentation updated
☐ Deployed to staging
☐ Product owner sign-off
```

### Team Collaboration Best Practices

#### 1. Comments
- Explain decisions and trade-offs
- Ask questions directly on issues
- Use @mentions for visibility
- Link related discussions

#### 2. Regular Updates
- Update status daily in standup
- Comment when moving between statuses
- Set accurate time tracking
- Update estimates if needed

#### 3. Timely Communication
- Notify blockers immediately
- Tag stakeholders in comments
- Use watchers for awareness
- Don't let issues go stale

### Workflow Best Practices

#### 1. Process Definition
- Document workflow in wiki
- Train team on transitions
- Define "Definition of Ready"
- Define "Definition of Done"

#### 2. Status Clarity
```
To Do:     Not started, in backlog
In Progress: Actively being worked on
In Review:   Code review/QA phase
Done:       Complete and deployed
Blocked:    Waiting on external factor
```

#### 3. Workflow Automation
- Auto-transition complete subtasks
- Close resolved issues after review
- Link related issues automatically
- Create follow-up tasks

### Reporting Best Practices

#### 1. Regular Metrics Review
- Sprint velocity trend
- Bug escape rate
- Mean time to resolution
- Release readiness

#### 2. Burndown Analysis
- Investigate unusual patterns
- Discuss scope creep
- Track team velocity
- Predict sprint completion

#### 3. Backlog Health
- Regular refinement meetings
- Remove duplicate issues
- Groom stories for next sprints
- Keep priorities current

