## Common Use Cases

### Bug Tracking Workflow
```
1. Bug reported → Priority assessed
2. Assigned → Investigation starts
3. Root cause found → Solution designed
4. Fix implemented → Code reviewed
5. Tested → Released to production
6. Verified fixed → Closed
```

### Feature Development Cycle
```
1. Requirement → Epic created
2. User stories written → Estimated
3. Sprint planning → Committed
4. Development → Code review
5. QA testing → Product review
6. Release → Monitor
7. Post-release → Improve if needed
```

### Release Management
```
Epic encompassing version
├── Story: Database migrations
├── Story: New features (1-5)
├── Story: Bug fixes (1-10)
├── Task: Release notes
└── Task: Deployment checklist
```

### Incident Management
```
Incident created (High priority)
→ Root cause analysis (Subtasks)
→ Fix implemented
→ Testing completed
→ Deployed
→ Post-incident review
→ Closed
```

