#### Q4: What is a Workflow and why do we need custom workflows?

**Conceptual explanation with scenarios:**
```
Workflow Definition:
A state machine defining how issues move through states
and what actions are allowed at each state.

Basic example:
New → Analysis → Development → Testing → Done

Why custom workflows needed?

Different issue types need different paths:

Bug workflow (fast):
New → Analyzing → In Progress → Testing → Done
└─ Fast track for hotfixes: Blocked → In Progress

Feature workflow (structured):
New → Analysis → Design → Development → Code Review → Testing → Done
└─ Design gate ensures quality requirements

Support task workflow (flexible):
New → Assigned → In Progress → Waiting Customer → In Progress → Done

Why not use same workflow for all?
├─ Bugs need rapid assessment (may not need design phase)
├─ Features need quality gates (need design review)
├─ Support needs flexibility (customer dependent)
└─ Tasks can be simple (no testing phase needed)

Real example from experience:
"When we treated bugs like stories (required design review),
critical bugs were delayed by 3 days. When we created a separate
bug workflow with fast track option, critical bugs were fixed
within 24 hours. Custom workflows reduced bug resolution time by 60%."

Technical implementation:

Workflow permissions control WHO can transition:
├─ Developer: Code → Code Review (submit for review)
├─ Tech Lead: Code Review → Approved (approve code)
├─ QA: Approved → Testing (start testing)
├─ QA: Testing → Done (confirm test pass)
└─ Manager: Any state → Blocked (identify blockers)

Validators ensure WHEN transition is allowed:
├─ "Code Review" requires: Code committed, Tests added
├─ "Testing" requires: Code merged, Staging deployed
├─ "Done" requires: QA sign-off, Documentation updated

Post-functions execute AFTER transition:
├─ On "Code Review": Send notification, Create code review task
├─ On "Testing": Deploy to staging, Run test suite
├─ On "Done": Deploy to production, Create release note

In interviews, emphasize:
- Workflows encode process into system
- Different flows for different work types
- Automation reduces manual steps
- Clear expectations prevent mistakes
```

