### Section 4: Technical Depth Questions

#### Q7: How would you design JIRA for a distributed, asynchronous team?

**Architectural answer:**
```
Challenges of distributed async teams:
├─ Time zone overlap may be minimal
├─ Synchronous meetings very difficult
├─ Assumptions about status become stale
├─ Context gets lost without synchronous discussion
└─ Escalation and unblocking takes longer

Design principles:

1. Asynchronous Communication First
   ├─ JIRA comments are primary communication
   ├─ Every decision documented in issue
   ├─ No "decision made in Slack" that's not in JIRA
   ├─ Thread discussions in JIRA, not side channels
   └─ @mentions are notifications, not interrupts

   Implementation:
   ├─ Enforce comment discipline
   ├─ Create comment templates:
   │  - When changing status
   │  - When requesting review
   │  - When blocked
   │  - When providing update
   │
   └─ Example:
      "Day 3 update: Implementation 70% complete.
       Discovered edge case in error handling.
       Timeline: +1 day expected. No blockers.
       Next: Code review Monday. @john-lead"

2. Clear ownership and responsibility
   ├─ Every issue has single assignee (not team)
   ├─ Assignee responsible for updates
   ├─ Status reflects truth (updated daily minimum)
   ├─ Async reviews assigned (not "code review")
   └─ Clear timeline expectations (done by when?)

3. Documentation replaces sync meetings
   ├─ Design decisions documented in issue
   ├─ Alternatives explored in comments
   ├─ Rationale explained (why this choice)
   ├─ Dissenting opinions captured
   └─ No "surprise" changes later

   Examples:
   - Architecture decision: Document in epic
   - API design: Full spec in API-design story
   - Testing strategy: Document before sprint

4. Proactive status updates
   ├─ Don't wait for question
   ├─ Update every day (at least)
   ├─ Include: Progress, blockers, timeline
   ├─ Highlight risks early
   └─ Escalate issues immediately

   JIRA automation:
   └─ Daily reminder comment template:
      "Day 4: Completed [what]. Working on [what].
       Blockers: [none or describe]. Timeline: [still on track or not].
       Help needed: [yes/no]. @watchers"

5. Time zone awareness
   ├─ Don't expect response same day
   ├─ Document decisions → let people review later
   ├─ Make deadlines with buffer for time zones
   └─ Escalation paths for urgent unblocking

   Example:
   ├─ Decision needed by Friday EOD
   ├─ Comment posted Monday EOD (time zone aware)
   ├─ People have Wed-Thu to review
   ├─ If not finalized by Thu EOD, escalate

6. Reduced meeting overhead
   ├─ Async standups in JIRA (comments not meetings)
   ├─ Backlog refinement: Written discussion first
   ├─ Planning: Async voting if possible
   ├─ Only sync meeting: Sprint demo (necessary)

   JIRA implementation:
   └─ Sprint planning flow:
      1. PM ranks backlog in JIRA (2 days)
      2. Team comments on stories (2 days)
      3. Team votes on estimates (emoji reactions)
      4. 30-min sync: Discuss high-variance votes
      5. PM confirms commitment in JIRA

7. Visibility dashboards
   ├─ Public daily status dashboard
   ├─ Shows: Progress, blockers, risks
   ├─ Accessible to all (time zone friendly)
   ├─ No need for status reports
   └─ Transparency builds trust

   Dashboard includes:
   ├─ Burndown chart (real-time)
   ├─ Open blockers (>1 day old highlighted)
   ├─ At-risk stories (late vs estimate)
   ├─ Upcoming deadlines
   └─ Velocity trend

8. Explicit escalation paths
   ├─ Blocker sitting > 1 day: Escalate to lead
   ├─ Decision needed: Tag owner explicitly
   ├─ Risk emerging: Create issue, notify PM
   ├─ Deadline slipping: Notify stakeholders early
   └─ No surprises (proactive communication)

   JIRA rules:
   └─ If: Blocker status > 1 day
      Then: Auto-comment escalation notice
            Add label "ESCALATED"
            Notify tech lead

9. Knowledge preservation
   ├─ Everything documented in JIRA (not Slack)
   ├─ Decision history visible
   ├─ New team members learn from issues
   ├─ No institutional knowledge loss
   └─ Reviews possible without people present

   Requirement:
   ├─ Every decision: Documented with rationale
