#### Q9: What are the biggest mistakes teams make with JIRA?

**Insightful answer based on experience:**
```
Top 5 mistakes:

1. Not using JIRA (treating it like optional)
   └─ Problem:
      ├─ Information scattered across channels
      ├─ No single source of truth
      ├─ Progress invisible
      ├─ Context lost
      └─ Onboarding difficult
   
   Solution:
   ├─ Make JIRA mandatory for all work
   ├─ Block work not tracked in JIRA
   ├─ Integrate JIRA into daily workflow
   └─ Measure: All work items tracked

2. Poor estimation culture
   └─ Problem:
      ├─ Estimates are guesses not plans
      ├─ Velocity meaningless
      ├─ Commitments unrealistic
      ├─ Morale suffers (always miss targets)
      └─ No basis for prediction
   
   Solution:
   ├─ Train team on story points
   ├─ Use historical data for calibration
   ├─ Celebrate accuracy (not optimism)
   ├─ Revisit estimates during development
   ├─ Measure: Estimation variance < 30%

3. Status not updated
   └─ Problem:
      ├─ Burndown chart is fiction
      ├─ Dashboard is yesterday's news
      ├─ Blockers not visible
      ├─ Planning based on assumptions
      └─ Surprises at sprint end
   
   Solution:
   ├─ Daily status update required
   ├─ Status = actual state (not aspiration)
   ├─ Comments on every transition
   ├─ Blockers flagged immediately
   ├─ Measure: 95%+ daily updates

4. Insufficient grooming
   └─ Problem:
      ├─ Stories unclear or vague
      ├─ Team wastes time clarifying
      ├─ Estimation impossible
      ├─ Sprint planning chaotic
      └─ Rework required mid-sprint
   
   Solution:
   ├─ Mandatory backlog refinement meeting
   ├─ Clear Definition of Ready checklist
   ├─ Acceptance criteria non-negotiable
   ├─ Tech lead pre-review stories
   ├─ Measure: 0 "Ready for Ready" issues in sprint

5. Ignoring the data
   └─ Problem:
      ├─ Velocity trends ignored
      ├─ Burndown problems not addressed
      ├─ Same mistakes repeated
      ├─ Decisions not data-driven
      └─ Team doesn't improve
   
   Solution:
   ├─ Weekly metrics review
   ├─ Dashboard visible to all
   ├─ Retrospectives analyze data
   ├─ Act on trends (don't ignore)
   ├─ Measure: Metrics improve each sprint

Other common mistakes:

6. Too many fields / complexity
   ├─ Cognitive load too high
   ├─ Team resists using JIRA
   └─ Solution: Start simple, add fields as needed

7. No clear workflow
   ├─ Statuses confusing
   ├─ Unknown who should do what
   └─ Solution: Clear workflow, training, enforcement

8. Communication in Slack, not JIRA
   ├─ Decisions not documented
   ├─ New team members lost
   └─ Solution: Comments in JIRA required

9. No enforcement
   ├─ Process optional
   ├─ Chaos results
   └─ Solution: Make following process non-optional

10. JIRA seen as overhead
    ├─ Team resents time updating
    ├─ Low adoption
    └─ Solution: Show ROI (less meeting time, clearer planning)
```

