#### Working with JIRA as a Developer

**Creating Issues**
```
When to create:
├─ Found a bug: Create bug immediately
├─ New requirement: Create story (if PM didn't)
├─ Blocker: Create if external or unknown
├─ Technical task: Create if necessary work emerges
└─ Follow-up: Create for related work discovered

Best practices:
├─ Title: Specific, searchable, clear
├─ Description: Include steps to reproduce (bugs)
├─ Labels: Add tags (security, performance, refactor)
├─ Link: To related issues
└─ Mention: Relevant people
```

**Estimating Stories**
```
Your perspective:
├─ Story points = YOUR effort estimate
├─ Based on: Complexity, unknowns, integration
├─ Include: Testing, code review, deployment
└─ Don't be optimistic: Assume normal interruptions

Estimation process:
1. Read story carefully
   ├─ Understand requirements
   ├─ Identify acceptance criteria
   ├─ Note any unknowns
   └─ Ask clarifying questions

2. Estimate effort
   ├─ What's the complexity?
   ├─ How many parts involved?
   ├─ Any unknowns that need research?
   ├─ Will I need help/review?
   └─ Realistic time needed?

3. Reference past work
   ├─ Similar story last sprint?
   ├─ What was actual effort?
   ├─ Adjust for differences
   └─ Use data, not gut feel

4. Commit to team estimate
   ├─ Discuss with team
   ├─ Team perspective may be different
   ├─ Agree on shared estimate
   └─ Everyone uses same scale

5. During sprint
   ├─ Track actual time
   ├─ If going over: Update estimate, flag early
   ├─ If finishing early: Help others, don't pack features
   └─ Provide feedback for next estimation
```

**Working on Assigned Issues**
```
Issue picked up:
1. Transition to "In Progress"
   └─ Comment: "Starting work. Design approach: [brief]. ETC: [when]"

2. As you work:
   ├─ Create sub-tasks for discovered work
   ├─ Update remaining estimate if needed
   ├─ Flag blockers immediately
   ├─ Link related issues
   └─ Daily update comment

3. Code review ready:
   ├─ Transition to "Code Review"
   ├─ Comment: "Ready for review. See PR #123. Key changes: [list]"
   ├─ Link pull request
   ├─ Mention reviewers
   └─ Add test summary

4. Addressing review feedback:
   ├─ Comment in JIRA: "Addressing feedback"
   ├─ Make changes in code
   ├─ Request re-review
   └─ Repeat until approved

5. Moving to testing:
   ├─ Transition to "Testing"
   ├─ Comment: "Ready for QA. Deployed to staging at [URL]"
   ├─ Mention QA team
   ├─ Include test scenarios
   └─ Provide any test data needed

6. Issue completed:
   ├─ Transition to "Done"
   ├─ Comment: "Deployed to production. Verified working."
   └─ Link to production verification if needed
