#### Dealing with Blockers

**When You're Blocked**
```
Blocker types:
├─ Waiting on another team (API not ready)
├─ Waiting on decision (design not approved)
├─ Technical blocker (missing dependency)
├─ Information blocker (requirement unclear)
└─ External blocker (vendor delay)

Immediate action:
1. Create or link blocking issue
   ├─ PROJ-123: "Blocked by BACKEND-456"
   ├─ Status: "Blocked"
   └─ Mark as blocker

2. Comment describing blocker
   └─ "Waiting for API endpoint /users/{id}/profile.
       Backend says ETA: Friday EOD.
       This blocks UI implementation.
       Workaround: Using mock data for now.
       Escalation: None needed yet, on track."

3. If critical:
   ├─ @mention person responsible
   ├─ Ask for ETA
   ├─ Suggest workaround if possible
   └─ Escalate if needed

4. Keep informed:
   ├─ Daily updates on blocker status
   ├─ Don't just wait silently
   ├─ Share workarounds with team
   └─ Help unblock others if you can

5. Workarounds:
   ├─ Mock data (for testing UI)
   ├─ Stub implementation (for integration testing)
   ├─ Split story (do what you can, defer rest)
   └─ Switch to different work (if flexible)

Resolution:
├─ When blocker removed: Comment "Blocker resolved"
├─ Transition from "Blocked" to previous status
├─ Continue work
└─ If moved, thank person who unblocked you
```

**When You're Blocking Others**
```
You're blocking someone if:
├─ You promised code review (not done)
├─ You promised API endpoint (not ready)
├─ You promised design (not approved)
├─ You promised decision (delayed)
└─ Someone linked issue as "blocked by" yours

Responsibilities:
├─ Know who you're blocking
├─ Give realistic ETAs
├─ Update status daily
├─ Help find workarounds if delayed
└─ Escalate if you'll miss deadline

Example:
Issue: PROJ-456 is blocked by your API work (PROJ-400)

You commit: "API endpoint done Friday EOD"

Daily updates:
├─ Mon: "Started design, on track for Friday"
├─ Wed: "Implementation 70%, still Friday"
├─ Thu: "Testing, looks good, Friday confirmed"
├─ Fri AM: "API merged to main"
└─ Fri PM: "Deployed to staging, ready for use"

If you get delayed:
├─ Tell blocker ASAP (don't wait until Friday)
├─ Comment: "Running behind. Now Tuesday instead of Friday.
            Workaround available (mock endpoint).
            Need help? Let me know."
├─ Give new ETA with confidence
├─ Daily updates to new ETA
└─ Escalate if still delayed
```

