#### Sprint Retrospectives

**Retrospective Process (90 minutes)**
```
Goal: Identify what went well, what didn't, what to improve

Setup (before meeting):
├─ Create JIRA issue: "Sprint 23 Retrospective"
├─ Prepare template with sections:
│  ├─ What went well?
│  ├─ What didn't go well?
│  ├─ What should we improve?
│  ├─ Action items
│  └─ Team sentiment
│
└─ Share link with team

Timing (90 minutes):
├─ 0-5 min: Setup and expectations
├─ 5-15 min: "What went well" brainstorm (10 min silence + discussion)
├─ 15-25 min: "What didn't go well" brainstorm
├─ 25-40 min: Root cause analysis (why?)
├─ 40-70 min: "What should improve" and solutions
├─ 70-85 min: Action items (owner, timeline, priority)
└─ 85-90 min: Team sentiment and close

Facilitation tips:

"What went well?"
└─ Start with positives (builds morale)
└─ Ask: "What are we proud of?"
└─ Examples:
   "PROJ-504 was fixed quickly" → Good triage process
   "Team was responsive" → Good communication
   "Daily standups helped" → Good practice
   "Sarah mentored John" → Good culture

"What didn't go well?"
└─ Create psychologically safe space
└─ Ask: "What frustrated us?"
└─ Listen without judgment
└─ Examples:
   "PROJ-505 was blocked 4 days" → Dependency issue
   "Estimation was off by 50%" → Process issue
   "Code review took forever" → Capacity issue
   "Unclear requirements" → Communication issue

Root cause analysis:
├─ For each problem: Ask "Why?"
├─ Then ask "Why?" again
├─ Then ask "Why?" once more
├─ Get to actual cause, not symptom
│
├─ Symptom: "Story took twice as long"
│  Why? "Requirements unclear"
│  Why? "Not discussed in refinement"
│  Why? "Refinement was rushed"
│  Root: Need more time for backlog refinement

"What should improve?"
└─ Brainstorm ideas
└─ Vote on top 3 ideas
└─ For each idea: "How do we implement?"
└─ Examples:
   "Add 1 hour refinement every Wednesday"
   "Code review SLA: Review within 4 hours"
   "Sprint size: Commit 15% buffer"
   "Pair programming for complex stories"

Action items:
├─ Not vague: "Improve communication" (bad)
├─ But specific: "Add 1 hour refinement every Wed" (good)
├─ Owner: "Sarah will run refinement"
├─ Timeline: "Starting next sprint"
├─ Success metric: "100% of stories ready by Friday"
├─ Follow-up: "Review in retro in 4 sprints"

