#### Backlog Refinement Facilitation

**Weekly Refinement Session (2 hours)**
```
Purpose:
├─ Prepare stories for next sprint planning
├─ Ensure team understands requirements
├─ Estimate complexity
├─ Identify risks and dependencies
└─ Quality gate before sprint starts

Preparation (SM before meeting):
├─ Compile backlog (PM ranked, top 15-20 stories)
├─ Verify: Each story has description
├─ Verify: PM has prioritized
├─ Prepare: Definition of Ready checklist
├─ Send: Backlog link to team (1 day early)
└─ Communicate: "Read top 10 stories before meeting"

Session structure (120 minutes):

0-10 min: Context
├─ "Here's the roadmap direction"
├─ "Here's why these stories matter"
├─ "Let's aim for 15-20 stories refined"
└─ "Focus: Top 10, detail on top 5"

10-100 min: Story discussion (5-8 min per story)
├─ Story 1 (PROJ-123): User Profile Settings
│  ├─ PM: "Here's what we want"
│  ├─ Team: Questions? Unclear parts?
│  ├─ Team: What complexity do you see?
│  ├─ Tech: Any architecture questions?
│  ├─ Update: Acceptance criteria based on discussion
│  └─ Estimate: Range (3-5 pts? 5-8 pts?)
│
├─ Story 2: Similar process
├─ Story 3: Similar process
└─ [Continue for top stories]

100-110 min: Dependency analysis
├─ "Which stories depend on others?"
├─ "Which stories block other teams?"
├─ "What needs to happen first?"
├─ Link issues: "PROJ-123 needed before PROJ-124"
└─ Timeline: "We'll do API design before UI implementation"

110-120 min: Summary and confirmation
├─ "Top 5 stories clear? Ready for planning?"
├─ "Any blockers we need to resolve?"
├─ "Next week we'll plan these, good?"
├─ Confirm: Team feels prepared
└─ Close: "Great work everyone"

Definition of Ready checklist:
For each story to be "refined":
☐ User story format clear
☐ Acceptance criteria defined (specific, testable)
☐ Dependencies identified
☐ Unknowns called out explicitly
☐ Design approved (if applicable)
☐ No questions remaining from team
☐ Complexity understood (rough points range)
☐ PM considers business value clear
☐ Tech lead sees no architecture blockers
☐ QA understands test scenarios

In JIRA:
├─ Create "Refined" label
├─ Add to refined stories
├─ Filter: Backlog AND label=Refined (ready for planning)
└─ Count refined: Track quality over time

SM responsibilities:
├─ Keep discussion focused
├─ Ensure everyone heard
├─ Ask clarifying questions
├─ Write better acceptance criteria
├─ Identify risks early
├─ Time-box discussions (5-8 min per story)
└─ Get to decisions (don't overthink)

Red flags to watch:
├─ Story has no acceptance criteria → Stop, define
├─ Team has major unknowns → Spike needed
├─ Dependency unclear → Link and document
├─ Disagreement on priority → Escalate to PM
├─ Over-detailed discussion → Save for implementation
└─ Multiple stories need same component → Batch

Follow-up (in JIRA):
├─ Update: All refined stories with details
├─ Add: Refined label to ready stories
├─ Create: Spike stories for unknowns
├─ Document: Dependencies in issue links
└─ Notify: "Backlog refined, planning Friday"
```

