#### Metrics and Dashboards for Scrum Masters

**Key JIRA Metrics to Track**
```
Velocity:
├─ Definition: Story points completed per sprint
├─ Goal: Stable (variance < 30%)
├─ Trend: Track last 6 sprints
├─ Use: Predict sprint capacity
│
├─ Example:
│  Sprint 18: 20 pts
│  Sprint 19: 22 pts
│  Sprint 20: 18 pts
│  Sprint 21: 21 pts
│  Sprint 22: 19 pts
│  Sprint 23: 20 pts
│  Average: 20 pts (stable ✓)
│
└─ Action: If variance > 30%, investigate

Cycle time:
├─ Definition: Days from story creation to Done
├─ Goal: Decreasing (faster delivery)
├─ Measure: "When created to when completed"
│
├─ Example:
│  Sprint 22: Average 8 days
│  Sprint 23: Average 7.5 days
│  Trend: ✓ Improving (1-2 hours per sprint)
│
└─ Action: If increasing, find bottleneck

Burndown accuracy:
├─ Definition: Actual burn vs committed velocity
├─ Goal: Actual ≈ Committed (±10%)
├─ Measure: "Did we finish what we committed?"
│
├─ Example:
│  Sprint 22: Committed 20, finished 19 (95%)
│  Sprint 23: Committed 20, finished 21 (105%)
│  Sprint 24: Committed 20, finished 15 (75%) ⚠
│  Trend: Last sprint was problem
│
└─ Action: If < 80%, discuss in retro

Code review turnaround:
├─ Definition: Hours from PR creation to review
├─ Goal: < 4 hours (same day review)
├─ Measure: Track in JIRA comments
│
├─ Example:
│  Avg turnaround: 6 hours
│  Goal: < 4 hours
│  Current: ⚠ Above goal
│
└─ Action: Add code review to Definition of Done

Bug escape rate:
├─ Definition: Bugs found in production vs QA
├─ Goal: < 10% (QA catches most bugs)
├─ Measure: Count bugs by source
│
├─ Example:
│  Bugs found in QA: 45
│  Bugs found in production: 8
│  Escape rate: 8/53 = 15% ⚠
│  Goal: < 10%
│
└─ Action: Improve QA process

Blocker duration:
├─ Definition: Days issue stays "Blocked"
├─ Goal: < 1 day (fast unblocking)
├─ Measure: "Blocked" to "resolved blocker"
│
├─ Example:
│  Sprint 22: Avg blocker duration 1.2 days
│  Sprint 23: Avg blocker duration 2.1 days ⚠
│  Trend: Worsening
│
└─ Action: Escalate blockers faster

Scope creep:
├─ Definition: New issues added mid-sprint
├─ Goal: < 10% of committed points (no surprises)
├─ Measure: "Issues created during sprint vs committed"
│
├─ Example:
│  Sprint 23: Committed 20 pts
│  Issues added mid-sprint: 3 pts
│  Scope creep: 15% ⚠
│  Goal: < 10% (2 pts)
│
└─ Action: Tighten sprint boundaries

