**Q9: How do you manage dependencies between teams in JIRA?**

A:
```
Scenario: Frontend blocked by Backend API

Setup in JIRA:

1. Create issues in separate projects
   ├─ FRONTEND-200: Login UI
   ├─ BACKEND-300: Login API endpoint
   └─ API-400: Login API specification

2. Link with dependency relationships
   ├─ FRONTEND-200 "blocks" BACKEND-300? No
   ├─ FRONTEND-200 "depends on" BACKEND-300? Yes
   ├─ FRONTEND-200 "is blocked by" API-400? Yes
   └─ Create explicit links

3. Timeline management
   ├─ Day 1-2: API-400 design and approval
   ├─ Day 3-5: BACKEND-300 implementation
   ├─ Day 3-5: FRONTEND-200 mock implementation
   ├─ Day 5: BACKEND-300 ready
   ├─ Day 6-7: FRONTEND-200 integrates real API
   └─ Day 8: Both teams test together

4. Status visibility
   ├─ Dashboard shows: API-400 in review (blocker)
   ├─ Dashboard shows: FRONTEND waiting (blocked)
   ├─ Weekly: Blocker resolution meeting
   ├─ Daily: Standup mentions dependencies
   └─ Clear escalation path if delayed

5. Communication
   ├─ JIRA links are the single source of truth
   ├─ Comments: Status updates on dependencies
   ├─ @mentions: Direct team attention
   ├─ Weekly sync: Cross-team coordination
   └─ No surprises (planned dependencies)

JIRA automation:
└─ If: Backend API moved to "Done"
   Then: Notify Frontend team
         Update dependency status
         Unblock Frontend story
```

