### Advanced Level Questions

**Q11: Design a JIRA workflow for a software team that does both features and support.**

A:
```
Challenge: Feature work (planned) vs Support (reactive)

Solution: Separate workflows for different work types

Feature workflow (for planned work):
New → Analysis → Design → Development → Testing → Done
└─ Allows time for planning and quality gates

Support workflow (for urgent issues):
New → Investigation → In Progress → Testing → Done
└─ Shorter, faster path (no design phase)

Bug workflow (for defects):
New → Analysis → Fix → Testing → Done
└─ Focused on quick resolution

Implementation in JIRA:

Project settings:
├─ Create workflows: Feature, Support, Bug
├─ Assign by issue type:
│  ├─ Story → Feature workflow
│  ├─ Task → Support workflow
│  └─ Bug → Bug workflow
│
├─ Permissions per workflow:
│  ├─ Feature: Design approval gate (Tech Lead required)
│  ├─ Support: Fast track if Highest priority
│  └─ Bug: Can skip QA if critical
│
└─ Automation rules:
   ├─ Feature: Block until design approved
   ├─ Support: Auto-assign to on-call
   └─ Bug: Email stakeholders on Done

Board configuration:
├─ Two swimlanes: Features and Support
├─ Features: Shows planned work
├─ Support: Shows reactive work
├─ Separate WIP limits:
│  ├─ Features: 5 items max
│  └─ Support: 2 items max

Capacity allocation:
├─ Team: 5 developers
├─ Allocation: 80% features, 20% support
├─ Sprint planning:
│  ├─ Commit features: 16 points
│  ├─ Leave buffer support: 4 points
│  └─ Team context switches okay

Team workflow:
├─ Support on-call rotates weekly
├─ On-call handles support issues
├─ Other 4 developers do features
├─ If support overloaded, feature dev helps
└─ Tracked in JIRA for metrics

Metrics:
├─ Feature velocity: 16 pts/sprint
├─ Support throughput: 8-10 issues/sprint
├─ Support cycle time: 2-3 days average
├─ Feature cycle time: 8-10 days average
└─ Both tracked separately on dashboard

Benefits:
✓ Clear paths for different work types
✓ Support doesn't derail feature work
✓ Capacity planning accurate
✓ Team satisfaction high
✓ Metrics show performance of both streams
```

