**Q13: A story got 50% through sprint with major unknowns discovered. What do you do?**

A:
```
Situation analysis:
├─ Story size: 5 points (estimated 2-3 days)
├─ Sprint elapsed: 5 days (sprint is 10 days)
├─ Progress: 50% done
├─ Discovery: "This is much more complex than thought"
├─ New estimate: 8-10 points
├─ Risk: Story won't finish this sprint

Decision framework:

Option 1: Push through (high risk)
├─ Keep working
├─ Hope to finish by sprint end
├─ Risk: Late night work, poor quality, burnout
├─ Result if fails: Missed commitment
└─ Decision: Usually bad idea

Option 2: Split the story (recommended)
├─ Identify: What's the absolute core?
├─ Do: Core functionality now (3 points remaining)
├─ Defer: Advanced features to next sprint (new story 3 points)
├─ Result: Finish core this sprint, extend scope next sprint
└─ Benefit: Meet commitment while capturing learning

Option 3: Descope from sprint (last resort)
├─ Move story to backlog
├─ Work on different story instead
├─ Document: Why and what was learned
├─ Risk: Negative team feeling ("we failed")
└─ Use when: Too much else is blocked

Implementation (using Option 2 - split):

In JIRA:

1. Update original story
   ├─ Rename: "User profile settings - Basic fields"
   ├─ Update estimate: 3 points remaining
   ├─ Reduce acceptance criteria: Keep only core
   ├─ Comment: "Splitting story to manage risk.
               Basic version now, advanced later."
   └─ Continue work on core

2. Create new story
   ├─ Name: "User profile settings - Advanced options"
   ├─ Estimate: 3 points
   ├─ Add to backlog (not this sprint)
   ├─ Link: "Related to PROJ-123"
   └─ Document: What was discovered

3. Team communication
   ├─ Comment in story: Situation and decision
   ├─ Update burndown (updated estimates)
   ├─ Standup: Explain split
   ├─ Message: "Good decision, we're being smart"
   └─ Benefit: Team feels confident

Timeline:
├─ Day 5: Discover complexity
├─ Day 5-6: Analyze and decide to split
├─ Day 6-8: Complete core functionality (3 pts)
├─ Sprint end: Core story done, advanced deferred
├─ Next sprint: Pick up advanced when bandwidth

Results:
✓ Original sprint goal met (core delivered)
✓ Learning captured (advanced story for later)
✓ Quality maintained (didn't rush)
✓ Team confidence high (smart decisions)
✓ No overtime required

Learning for process:
├─ "Profile settings" is complex area
├─ Future estimates include more buffer
├─ Better upfront research before sprint
├─ Better story splitting in planning
└─ Assign more experienced dev if needed
```

