**Q16: A critical production bug is reported Friday 4pm, needs fix by Monday. How do you use JIRA?**

A:
```
Immediate response (Friday 4pm):

1. Create urgent issue in JIRA
   ├─ Type: Bug (Critical)
   ├─ Priority: BLOCKER
   ├─ Title: "Production bug: [clear description]"
   ├─ Description: 
   │  ├─ What: Clear description
   │  ├─ Impact: How many customers/what broke
   │  ├─ Frequency: Every time? Intermittent?
   │  ├─ Workaround: Is there temporary fix?
   │  └─ When: When was it discovered?
   │
   └─ Assign: Senior developer with domain knowledge

2. Create war room
   ├─ Notify: Tech lead, on-call engineer, dev
   ├─ Start: Zoom/video discussion
   ├─ Goal: Understand and reproduce bug
   └─ JIRA: Link to incident command channel

3. Triage (30 minutes)
   ├─ Reproduce: Confirm it's real
   ├─ Scope: How many users affected
   ├─ Workaround: Can customers work around it?
   ├─ Root cause: Early hypothesis
   └─ JIRA update: "Confirmed. Triaged. Investigating..."

4. Investigation (2 hours)
   ├─ Check: Recent deployments, logs, metrics
   ├─ Hypothesis: Most likely cause
   ├─ Solution: Proposed fix
   └─ JIRA: Document findings, link to hypothesis

5. Decision (6pm)
   ├─ Fast fix possible? (Yes → proceed)
   ├─ Fast fix not possible? (Need broader fix)
   ├─ Hotfix or wait? (Depends on impact)
   ├─ Customer impact: Communicate ETA
   └─ JIRA: Decision documented, next steps clear

6. Resolution (weekend if needed)
   ├─ Code fix written
   ├─ Testing in staging
   ├─ Deploy: Careful, watch metrics
   ├─ JIRA: Update status "Deployed"
   └─ Verify: Bug actually fixed

Monday follow-up:

1. Post-incident review
   ├─ Why did bug happen?
   ├─ Why wasn't it caught before production?
   ├─ How do we prevent this class of bugs?
   └─ Create JIRA epic: "Prevent similar bugs"

2. Root cause analysis (JIRA issue)
   ├─ Timeline documented
   ├─ Decisions explained
   ├─ Learning captured
   └─ Action items created

3. Action items
   ├─ Better test coverage
   ├─ Improved monitoring
   ├─ Code review changes
   ├─ Deployment process changes
   └─ Team training

JIRA status progression:
```
Friday 4pm: NEW → URGENT TRIAGE
Friday 5pm: TRIAGING → INVESTIGATING
Friday 7pm: INVESTIGATING → CODING FIX
Friday 9pm: CODING FIX → TESTING
Saturday: TESTING → READY FOR DEPLOY
Saturday: READY FOR DEPLOY → DEPLOYED TO PROD
Monday: DEPLOYED → POST-INCIDENT REVIEW DONE

Final status: CLOSED (and lessons learned issue created)
```

Key principles:
├─ Speed of communication critical (not perfection)
├─ JIRA documents timeline and decisions
├─ Transparency to stakeholders
├─ Learning captured for future
└─ Team enabled to handle similar issues next time
```

